Rename or copy this file to `KILL_SWITCH` (no extension) to halt the system.

While runtime/KILL_SWITCH exists:
  * no new entries are generated or submitted
  * unfilled ENTRY orders are cancelled
  * protective exits (stops / reduce-only targets) are LEFT IN PLACE
  * existing positions are NOT force-closed -- use `flatten` for that, which
    needs FLATTEN_CONFIRMATION=CLOSE_ALL_POSITIONS

The switch is checked before every entry decision and on every loop tick, so
it takes effect within one cycle. Deleting the file re-arms entries; nothing
resumes automatically while it is present.
